# Prefer lookup maps over similar if-else

When several branches only differ by a **key → value** (or key → title/label/handler), do **not** grow a long `if` / `else if` ladder. Extract a map (or enum + map) and look up.

## Do

```tsx
const utilityTitles: Partial<Record<ShellView, string>> = {
  settings: t("settings.sidebar.title"),
  apps: t("settings.nav.apps", { defaultValue: "Apps" }),
  download: downloadTitle,
};
const utilityTitle = utilityTitles[view];
if (utilityTitle != null) {
  return t("app.documentTitle.chat", { title: utilityTitle });
}
// fallback for chat / unknown
```

## Don't

```tsx
if (view === "settings") { /* … */ return; }
if (view === "apps") { /* … */ return; }
if (view === "download") { /* … */ return; }
// …repeated nearly identical bodies
```

## When this applies

- Same shape of work in each branch (set title, pick label, pick icon, pick route segment, etc.)
- Discriminant is a string/union/`enum`-like view or status key
- Adding a new case should mean **one map entry**, not another `if` block

## When if-else is fine

- Branches have **different control flow** (early return vs throw vs side effects that are not isomorphic)
- Only **2** short branches and a map would be harder to read
- Conditions are not keyed by a stable discriminant (complex boolean logic)

Prefer `Partial<Record<UnionKey, T>>`, `Map`, or a small helper (`resolveX(key)`) colocated with the call site or in a domain constants module.
